## 🔹 What I Learned

### First-Class Functions

Functions can be stored in variables, passed as arguments, and returned from other functions.

### Higher-Order Functions

A function can accept another function as an argument or return another function.

### Lambda Functions

Small anonymous functions used for simple operations.

### `map()`

Applies a function to every item in an iterable.

### `filter()`

Selects items that satisfy a condition.

### `reduce()`

Combines multiple values into one final result.

##  Key Learning

```text
map()    → Transform items
filter() → Select items
reduce() → Combine items
```

